  "contentHtml": "\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <p><img src=\"https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/et-default-user.svg\" alt=\"Online Bureau\">\n                                            \n                                        </p>\n                                                                        \n                                                                                    <ul>\n                                                                                                    <li>\n                                                                                                                                                                            <a>Online Bureau</a>\n                                                            \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \n                                                                                                            </li>\n                                                                                                                                                    <li><a href=\"/agency/88675629/ETHealthWorld\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ETHealthWorld</a></li>\n                                                                                            </ul>\n                                                                                <ul>\n                                                                                            <li>Published On Nov 23, 2026 at 04:41 PM IST</li>\n                                                                                                                                </ul>\n                                    \n                                                                            \n                                                                        \n                                \n                                \n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p>Mumbai: <a href=\"/tag/robotic+surgical+systems\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Robotic Surgical Systems</a> market in India is set to grow at 13 per cent CAGR through 2036, Global Data forecasts.India is expected to account for nearly 6 per cent of the Asia-Pacific (APAC) robotic surgical systems devices market in 2026, with general surgery robotic surgical systems dominating the market at 94 per cent, according to Global Data's report titled “Robotic Surgical Systems Market Size by Segments, Share, Regulatory, Reimbursement, Installed Base and Forecast to 2036”</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>As per Global Data, robust growth in the market will be driven by rising demand for <a href=\"/tag/minimally+invasive+procedures\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">minimally invasive procedures</a>, increasing procedure volumes, and continued healthcare infrastructure investments.</p>\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>It also highlights advancements in technology, increased familiarity among surgeons, and the increasing use of robot-assisted surgery are prompting hospitals to expand capabilities across various surgical specialties as reasons for growth.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>It cited the introduction of advanced surgical systems like Intuitive’s da Vinci 5 at  Max Super Speciality Hospital in New Delhi and Nanavati Max Super Speciality Hospital in Mumbai as a significant step toward the adoption of next-generation robotic-assisted surgery in the country.Aakansha Pankaj, Medical Devices Analyst at GlobalData, comments: “The Indian surgical landscape is gradually shifting toward technology-enabled operating environments, where procedural precision, consistency, and surgeon control are becoming increasingly significant. Beyond the deployment of robotic platforms, the market’s long-term growth will depend on building surgeon skills, integration of robotic systems into standard surgical workflows, and demonstrating their clinical and operational value. Major hospital networks are expected to play an important role in advancing this shift, as they increase their investment in the technology.”</p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                                                            <!-- <li>By <span>Online Bureau</span>,</li> -->\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <li>By\n                                                                                            <a>Online Bureau</a>\n                                                                                                                                                                                        , \n                                                                                    </li>\n                                                                                                                <li><a href=\"/agency/88675629/ETHealthWorld\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ETHealthWorld</a></li>\n                                                                    </ul>\n  